 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+- `--delimiter` (short form `-d`) sets the field separator.
+
+### Deprecated
+- `--sep`: use `--delimiter` instead. `--sep` still works, with a warning on stderr.
+
 ## [1.0.0] - 2026-09-01
 
 ### Added
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 07fed77..723cd18 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,10 +5,11 @@ Prints delimited text as a Markdown table. The first row becomes the header.
 ## Usage
 
     python3 mdtable.py people.csv
-    python3 mdtable.py --sep ';' people.txt
-    cut -d: -f1,7 /etc/passwd | python3 mdtable.py --sep :
+    python3 mdtable.py --delimiter ';' people.txt
+    cut -d: -f1,7 /etc/passwd | python3 mdtable.py -d :
 
-`--sep` sets the field separator (default `,`).
+`--delimiter` (or `-d`) sets the field separator (default `,`). The old name, `--sep`, still
+works but is deprecated: it prints a warning and will be removed in a future release.
 
